# Screen Application

Moves an inbound **Application** into the hiring pipeline: it creates a **Candidate** in `screening` with the applicant's name, email, phone, photo, applied role and position, applied date and résumé, and marks the application `converted`. A free-text referrer name links the candidate's `referredBy` only when exactly one employee has that name, since linking the wrong person is worse than leaving it for a human.

```ts
import { ScreenApplicationCommand } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/hr/commands/screen-application-command';

let { candidate, message } = await new ScreenApplicationCommand(commandContext).execute({
  application,
});
```

Returns `{ candidate, message }`, so the caller can open the new Candidate straight away. It refuses an application that is already converted. The application stays as the record of what was submitted; the candidate is where the hiring work happens.

### Non-goals

No duplicate detection against existing candidates. No scoring of the résumé.
